\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S1}{\ignorespaces What the permutation test could have detected. One-sided exact $p$ for the mean-difference statistic as the incumbent simulants are moved $\delta $ typical nearest-neighbour separations closer to the eleven agents, with the rest of each panel unchanged and the null taken from the unmodified distances. On the primary panel the test crosses $\alpha = 0.05$ at $\delta = 0.23$. The shaded band spans that value and the median deficit the incumbent compounds actually carry, 0.493; the deficit falls below the detectable value only at sarin.}}{S-40}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mde}{{S1}{S-40}{}{}{}}
