\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S2}{\ignorespaces Every simulant designation we located, with the agent it names, the measurement it was made against, and the basis the designating document itself states. Source URLs and the search date are in \texttt  {sources/designations\_20261106.csv} of the deposit.}}{S-67}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:designations}{{S2}{S-67}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S3}{\ignorespaces The 29-component array, in the order the three source studies number it. Five entries marked $^{a}$ are not chromogenic dyes; $^{b}$ marks a component whose stock solvent differs between the source studies.}}{S-68}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:dyepanel}{{S3}{S-68}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S4}{\ignorespaces Every exact permutation test across panel constructions, descriptor spaces and statistics. Values are one-sided $p$. Bold marks $p<0.05$ before correction. The last column is the smallest Benjamini--Hochberg value over the eighteen tests of that panel construction. Dimensions are the retained coordinate counts after the correlation filter of Section~\ref {meth:orderinvariance}.}}{S-69}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ablation}{{S4}{S-69}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S5}{\ignorespaces Six ways of accounting for the search, applied to the eighteen tests of each panel configuration. The Westfall-Young min-$P$ value \mciteCiteA  {\@auxout }{main}{\relax }{\relax }{\cite }{westfall1993} is exact for the dependence among the tests, since all eighteen share one enumeration of designations; $m_{\mathrm  {eff}}$ approximates that dependence from the eigenvalues of the correlation matrix of the eighteen nulls \mciteCiteA  {\@auxout }{main}{\relax }{\relax }{\cite }{liji2005}, used as a Bonferroni divisor. On the primary panel no scheme returns anything below 0.05 and on the smaller panel only the pre-specified-statistic scheme does, while the fourth configuration, which differs from the second by two class labels, is below 0.05 under every scheme.}}{S-69}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:family}{{S5}{S-69}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S6}{\ignorespaces Adopted vapour pressures for the twenty-eight-compound panel, in descending order. Values are measurements retrieved from PubChem, which carries them from the Hazardous Substances Data Bank and from the government compendia named in the source column; the adoption rule and the tier definitions are in the text. No value was converted between temperatures.}}{S-70}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:volatility}{{S6}{S-70}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S7}{\ignorespaces What each agent is nearest to on the volatility axis. The series column is the agent's own class. For three of the eleven agents the nearest compound in the pool is an interferent rather than a simulant. This table is descriptive and enters no multiplicity accounting.}}{S-71}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:vpairing}{{S7}{S-71}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S8}{\ignorespaces Equal weight per descriptor against equal weight per block, in the merged space. Valid-match counts are identical under the two weightings on every panel construction. The smallest $p$ is taken over the eighteen-test family of three spaces by six statistics, and $q$ is the Benjamini--Hochberg adjusted value of that family.}}{S-71}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:blockbalance}{{S8}{S-71}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S9}{\ignorespaces Valid matches and the lewisite row across panel configurations (Section~\ref {sec:si-ascl3}). A match requires a normalised distance of at most two \emph  {and} that no non-simulant lies closer.}}{S-71}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:si-ascl3}{{S9}{S-71}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S10}{\ignorespaces GFN2-xTB local reactivity at phosphorus for the six phosphorus-bearing compounds. $f^{+}(\mathrm  {P})$ is the condensed Fukui index for nucleophilic attack at phosphorus, in the frontier-electron formulation of Parr and Yang\mciteCiteA  {\@auxout }{main}{\relax }{\relax }{\cite }{parryang1984} with the atomic condensation of Yang and Mortier.\mciteCiteA  {\@auxout }{main}{\relax }{\relax }{\cite }{yangmortier1986} $\omega $ is the global electrophilicity index in the definition of Parr et al.~\mciteCiteA  {\@auxout }{main}{\relax }{\relax }{\cite }{parr1999} with $\eta $ equal to half the HOMO--LUMO gap, and $\omega _k = \omega f^{+}(\mathrm  {P})$ is the composite local electrophilicity of Domingo et al.~\mciteCiteA  {\@auxout }{main}{\relax }{\relax }{\cite }{domingo2016}. The two reactivity conventions disagree about VX and the text says why.}}{S-72}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:plocal}{{S10}{S-72}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S11}{\ignorespaces Premise test under the label-permutation null. The statistic is the mean over compounds of (agreement with itself across concentrations) minus (agreement with the other compounds' consensus patterns). The null permutes compound labels within each concentration. Fixing the first concentration's labels leaves $(n!)^{C-1}$ distinct relabellings, which is enumerable for the four-compound set and sampled for the others.}}{S-72}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:premisenull}{{S11}{S-72}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S12}{\ignorespaces Regulatory acute inhalation values held for the three incumbent simulants, by register. Sources and collection dates are in \texttt  {sources/registers\_20261106.csv} of the deposit. EPA AEGL is the axis the agents are placed on in the main text; the other registers use different averaging times and severity definitions and are not interchangeable with it.}}{S-73}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:registers}{{S12}{S-73}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S13}{\ignorespaces Decoupling test. Fidelity is the standardised electronic-space distance to the nearest authentic agent; safety is the measured EPA AEGL-3 (10~min).}}{S-73}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:h1}{{S13}{S-73}{}{}{}}
